.TH SWIFTKHD 1 "April 2026" "SwiftKHD 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swiftkhd \- Simple Hotkey Daemon for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swiftkhd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swiftkhd
is a simple hotkey daemon for macOS, written in Swift.
It is a compatible port of
.BR skhd (1),
sharing the same configuration file format and supporting modal hotkeys,
process-specific bindings, key forwarding, and media key intercept.
.PP
Service management uses the native SMAppService API (macOS 13+).
The daemon runs in the background and monitors a configuration file,
applying key bindings while optionally hot-reloading changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " file" ", --config " file
Use \fIfile\fR as the configuration file instead of the default search path.
.TP
.B \-V , --verbose
Enable verbose logging.
.TP
.B \-h , --no-hotload
Disable automatic config reload when the file changes on disk.
.TP
.B \-o , --observe
Observe mode: print raw keyboard events to stdout without applying any bindings.
Useful for discovering key names and modifiers to use in a config file.
Press Ctrl-C to exit.
.TP
.B \-P , --profile
Enable profiling and tracing output.
.TP
.BI \-k " keyspec" ", --key " keyspec
Synthesize a keypress described by \fIkeyspec\fR (e.g.\& \fBcmd\ \-\ a\fR) and exit.
Does not start the daemon.
.TP
.BI \-t " text" ", --text " text
Synthesize keyboard input of \fItext\fR and exit.
Does not start the daemon.
.TP
.B \-r , --reload
Send a reload signal to the running swiftkhd instance.
.TP
.B --install-service
Register swiftkhd as a launchd login item using SMAppService.
.TP
.B --uninstall-service
Unregister the launchd service.
.TP
.B --start-service
Start the launchd service.
.TP
.B --stop-service
Stop the launchd service.
.TP
.B --restart-service
Restart the launchd service.
.TP
.B --status
Print the current launchd service status.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version number and exit.
.SH FILES
When no
.B \-\-config
is given, swiftkhd searches for a configuration file in the following order:
.PP
.RS
.PD 0
.TP
1.
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/skhd/skhdrc
.TP
2.
.I ~/.config/skhd/skhdrc
.TP
3.
.I ~/.skhdrc
.TP
4.
.I ./skhdrc
(current directory)
.PD
.RE
.PP
If no file is found, swiftkhd prompts to create a default config at
.IR ~/.config/skhd/skhdrc .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Bindings follow the format:
.PP
.RS
[\fImodifier\fR +] [\fImodifier\fR] \fB\-\fR \fIkey\fR \fB:\fR \fIcommand\fR
.RE
.PP
Modifiers: \fBcmd\fR, \fBalt\fR, \fBshift\fR, \fBctrl\fR, \fBfn\fR.
Keys are named identifiers such as
.BR return ", " space ", " a \- z ", " 0 \- 9 ", " f1 \- f20 .
.PP
Media and system keys (\fBplay\fR, \fBnext\fR, \fBprevious\fR, \fBmute\fR,
\fBsound_up\fR, \fBsound_down\fR, \fBrewind\fR, \fBfast\fR) do not require
modifiers and are written directly as the key name.
.PP
Use
.B \-\-observe
to print key names for any key you press.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the daemon using the default config:
.PP
.RS
.B swiftkhd
.RE
.PP
Start with a specific config file:
.PP
.RS
.B swiftkhd \-c ~/.config/skhd/skhdrc
.RE
.PP
Discover key names interactively:
.PP
.RS
.B swiftkhd \-\-observe
.RE
.PP
Synthesize a keypress from the command line:
.PP
.RS
.B swiftkhd \-k 'cmd \- a'
.RE
.PP
Install and start the background service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B swiftkhd \-\-install-service
.B swiftkhd \-\-start-service
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reload config after editing:
.PP
.RS
.B swiftkhd \-\-reload
.RE
.SH NOTES
.SS Function keys and macOS settings
By default, macOS maps the F1\(enF20 keys to system functions such as
brightness and volume control.
To bind
.BR f1 \(en f20
directly in a swiftkhd config, enable
.B System Settings \(-> Keyboard \(-> \[lq]Use F1, F2, etc. keys as standard function keys\[rq]
.PP
Alternatively, use the
.B fn
modifier in the binding to target the raw function key regardless of
the system setting:
.PP
.RS
.EX
fn - f1 : open -a Safari
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skhd (1)
.PP
